-- title:
--   Finite ideles surject onto the class group with kernel widehat R^× K^×
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Dedekind domain (a commutative ring satisfying `IsDedekindDomain`) and let $K$ be a field which is an $R$-algebra and a fraction field of $R$. The assertion is that there exists a monoid homomorphism $\varphi$ from the unit group $(\mathbb{A}_{R,K}^{f})^{\times}$ of the finite adele ring `FiniteAdeleRing R K` to the class group `ClassGroup R` such that: (i) $\varphi$ is surjective as a function, and (ii) the kernel of $\varphi$, as a subgroup of $(\mathbb{A}_{R,K}^{f})^{\times}$, is exactly the join (the subgroup generated by the union) of two subgroups, namely `unitIdeles R K` and the range of the map on unit groups induced by the algebra map $K \to \mathbb{A}_{R,K}^{f}$. Here `unitIdeles R K` is the subgroup consisting of those units $\delta$ such that for every $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $R$ the $v$-component of $\delta$ lies in the valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$ given by `v.adicCompletionIntegers K`, and likewise every $v$-component of $\delta^{-1}$ lies in $\mathcal{O}_v$; the second subgroup is the image of $K^{\times}$ in the idele group. Only existence of such a $\varphi$ is asserted: no formula for the homomorphism, and no normalisation of its values on uniformiser ideles, forms part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the classical exact sequence $1 \to \widehat{R}^{\times}K^{\times} \to (\mathbb{A}_K^{f})^{\times} \to \mathrm{Cl}(R) \to 1$, presenting the ideal class group as a quotient of the finite idele group by the unit ideles and the principal ideles, in existential form. It is used in the computation of Herbrand quotients and Tate cohomology of idele class groups, where the quotient description of $\mathrm{Cl}(R)$ transfers index and rank information from ideles to ideal classes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_FiniteAdeleRing_exists_monoidHom_units_classGroup_surjective_ker_eq.lean

